# BuildKit uses <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the repo-root one,
# so this file scopes the demo build's context without touching production.
#
# The root .dockerignore excludes everything and allowlists only the prebuilt
# target/quarkus-app — exactly right for the published image, but this build
# compiles from source and needs src/, pom.xml and the Maven wrapper.
#
# Excluded here: anything that would only slow the context upload or leak local
# state into the image.

.git/
.github/
target/
tmp/
.claude/
.idea/
*.iml
**/node_modules/
# The UIs are built INSIDE the image from ui/ (see Dockerfile.demo): the Node
# toolchain the Maven build downloads into ui/node, and local build output,
# must not leak in from the checkout.
ui/node/
ui/*/dist/
ui/*/.keycloak-test-realm/
ui/*/test-results/
ui/*/playwright-report/
*.log
.env
